particle_podcast_get_mention_trends: description, inputSchema  -whether the +a label. A -is +in both windows is `continuing`; one only in the previous is `dropped`. A show only in the current window is judged against the lookback before it (`lookback_days`, default 90): +when it never mentioned the subject there, published at least four episodes there, and has two or more mention lines now; `returning` when it mentioned the subject earlier in the lookback; `passing` for a single line; `newly_tracked` when it published too little in the lookback -the subject, `continuing`, or `dropped` it. +tell. -call. +call, and, with `change="new"` (sorted by popularity  parameters: +with this label. 'new': started talking about the subject: two or more mention lines in the window, none in the lookback before it, on a show -are 'new' +published at least four episodes there. Use it for 'which shows started talking about X' or 'mentioned X for the first time'. 'returning': back after a gap in the lookback. 'passing': a single line, a first in the lookback. 'newly_tracked': too little published history -the subject (current +tell (fewer than four episodes in the lookback, which includes a monthly show over the default 90 days: pass lookback_days=180 for those). 'continuing':
particle_podcast_get_rankings: description, inputSchema  -debuts, +entries, +Most `change=new` entries are established shows returning to the chart; for new podcasts, launches, or debuts use `change=debut` — shows on that chart slot for the first time since tracking began (May 2026). A debut is per slot: a show can debut on the overall chart after months in a category, so read its episode count and, when shown, its first-episode date before calling it brand-new. -time. +time, newest first. Per-podcast history defaults to `country=us`; pass `country` for other markets. For one chart's trajectory pass `source`, `country`, and `category_slug` too (omit  parameters: +'debut': shows on this chart slot for the first time since tracking began (May 2026) — use it for 'new podcasts', 'just launched', 'debuted'. 'new': every entry, mostly established shows returning. 'reentry': only the returning ones. +"debut", "reentry",

